# Copy this file to .dev.vars for local development with `wrangler dev`.
#
# In production, this value is never stored in git — it's set as a real
# Worker secret, either via `wrangler secret put BACKUP_TOKEN` or by
# filling in the field Cloudflare's "Deploy to Cloudflare" button shows
# you during setup (which reads this file to know what to ask for).
#
# Any long random string works. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# or paste one from a password generator. Save whatever you use here —
# you'll paste this same value into the extension's Settings > Cloud
# Backup > "Backup token" field.
BACKUP_TOKEN=replace-with-a-long-random-string
